<title>INDIA: BSE figures of India carry forward trade - Aug 31.</title>
<headline>BSE figures of India carry forward trade - Aug 31.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1996-09-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following is the latest data, for the top 10 stocks by value, released by the Bombay Stock Exchange (BSE) for the carry forward or &quot;badla&quot; account ended Aug 31.</p>
<p>SCRIP		  SETTLEMENT  AV BADLA  QTY    VALUE    % BADLA</p>
<p>			 RATE				 (RS MLN)</p>
<p>---------------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>Tata Steel	   196	   0.52     373550  73.22    13.83</p>
<p>Reliance	     211	   0.40     212650  44.87     9.88</p>
<p>L&amp;T		    255	   0.63     151500  38.63    12.88</p>
<p>ACC		   2157	   6.00	14310  30.87    14.50</p>
<p>Tata Power	   153	   0.40     185300  28.35    13.63</p>
<p>Tata Chem	    210	   0.54	62200  13.06    13.41</p>
<p>Tata Engg	    510	   0.61	23400  11.93     6.24</p>
<p>ICICI		   76	   0.17     137250  10.43    11.66</p>
<p>Hind Lever	   840	   1.40	 8700   7.31     8.69</p>
<p>Mah &amp; Mah	    360	   0.06	17450   6.28     0.87</p>
<p>---------------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>The average badla charges work out to 12.16 percent on an annualised basis against 15.10 percent in the previous carry forward account ended Aug 24.</p>
<p>-- Bombay newsroom +91-22-265 9000</p>
